I like the straw golem thing.

Slashem addresses the problem (perhaps accidentally?) by having molds
and lichens appear on sufficiently old corpses. Killing these provides
a great source of herbi/veggie-fodder.

I'd like to see grass as a dungeon feature in nethack: A green . that
can be either long grass (ready for grazing) or short grass (already
grazed). Short grass grows into long grass, but it takes a long while.
Snakes and scorpions and such can hide in long grass. Grass can be
turned into regular dungeon floor by dig&fill or by fire, and long
grass can even spread fire.  Maybe grass could be cut (using the
appropriate tool: Is there a "scythe" polearm in nethack?) to create a
source of straw, tying the straw golem patch into the game a little
more coherently.

Of course, you wouldn't find much grass in the dungeon- it'd be mostly
